{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqf516f3zz9","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Cost attribution must accumulate per task across agent run finishes, role tagged","summary":"Background Agent-tool workers spawned with run_in_background never reach the graph cost ledger: the SubagentStop hook does not fire for them, start_task self-registers the worker but carries no usage, so per task cost falls into the costflow unattributed bucket (verified: zero usage_records slices for the code-judge tasks despite ~160k output tokens). DESIGN: report on EVERY agent run finish, not only terminal complete_task, because the lifecycle is multi attempt — worker run plus impl tokens, then code judge run plus review tokens, then kick back, then another worker run, then another judge run, then complete. Reports must ACCUMULATE keyed by task key (today usage_records is keyed by agent id and overwrites, so it cannot sum across attempts), and each report is ROLE tagged implementation versus review so per task cost equals sum impl plus sum review and rework is visible. Unit stays output tokens. OPEN QUESTION (token source — a subagent cannot see its own count): preferred is the daemon parsing the agent transcript by agent id (reuses the existing usage normalize path, no trust on the agent to self count); fallback is the dispatcher relaying the harness reported subagent tokens on the completion notification. Prior art: note the done task on correlating subagent transcript with task assignee.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T11:36:36.543Z","vec":[-0.05600452423095703,-0.014917406253516674,-0.11352391541004181,0.003849806496873498,0.03465839847922325,-0.005264836363494396,0.029232380911707878,0.027399929240345955,0.07519037276506424,0.0788315162062645,-0.018529733642935753,-0.06083758920431137,0.04549475014209747,-0.0012000247370451689,-0.05357400327920914,0.017180293798446655,0.14634135365486145,-0.039094842970371246,-0.03733926638960838,-0.10066734254360199,0.05095